# Permissions

Owns the access vocabulary and enforcement model. Always enforce permission-based access;
deny by default.

## Key Format

- Keys are lowercase `resource:action`, each part snake_case — `clinical:write`,
  `rooms_beds:read`, `pricing:pharmacy_read`.
- Canonical catalog: `backend/src/config/permissions.js` (85 keys). The frontend mirrors it
  in `AppPermissions` (`frontend/lib/core/permissions/app_permission.dart`); parity is
  asserted by `frontend/test/core/permissions/app_permission_catalog_parity_test.dart`.
- Dot-notation (`billing.manage`) is not a permission key and must not appear anywhere.
- Shell entry uses exactly one `*:read` key per menu destination (`opd:read`). One key ↔
  one destination; never reuse an entry key for a second route.
- New keys must land in both catalogs before seeds, gates, or APIs use them.

## Vocabulary

- Core actions: `read`, `write`, `update`, `delete`, `manage`, `export`, `approve`,
  `publish`, `admin`, `audit`.
- Module-specific actions may be added (`request`, `review`, `release`, `manage_storage`).
- Prefer `own` / `assigned` ABAC scope over manage-all grants.
- Non-read actions imply their sibling read; `permission-read-dependency.js` expands them
  and blocks deselecting a read while sibling actions remain.

## Access Model

Effective access is a union of grants, then narrowed by three independent ceilings:

```
union(role packs ∪ module grants ∪ direct user grants)
  ∩ assigned modules          (module entitlement)
  ∩ subscription cap          (plan permission ceiling)
  ∩ ABAC scope                (evaluated in middleware/services)
  − version-disabled domains  (stripped for everyone)
```

Authority order is plan → role → rights. Owned by
`backend/src/lib/authorization/effective-access.js`; the client mirrors the same order in
`AppAccessPolicy.fromSession`.

- Users may hold multiple scoped roles via `user_role`; net rights are the **union** of
  every assigned role's pack, not the intersection.
- Grants must not exceed the active package or the actor's own ceiling.
- Version-disabled domains (`version-disabled-screens.mdc`) are stripped last, from all
  users and all packages, including platform-elevated paths that skip plan caps.

### Module-scoped vs core permissions

The plan gates only bite on **module-scoped** permissions — those whose domain maps to a
module in `permission-module-map.js`. 64 of the 85 keys are module-scoped.

The other 21 are core/platform and bypass both the module gate and the plan cap:

`profile:*`, `setup:read`, `access_admin:read`, `pricing:*`, `last_office:*`,
`compliance:*`, `break_glass:*`, `evidence:export`, `facility:admin`, `tenant:admin`,
`platform:admin`, `platform:owner`.

Consequences to keep in mind:

- Listing a core key in a plan cap is **inert** — it neither grants nor restricts. Do not
  add one; the caps test rejects it.
- `setup:read` and `access_admin:read` are not plan-gated. The admin surface is gated by
  role and by ABAC scope, not by package tier. Tier differences inside `/admin/setup`
  (tenant vs facility vs partial) come from role packs, not from the subscription.
- `reporting-analytics` is platform infrastructure and passes the module gate on every
  package, so `reports:read` is effectively universal for any user holding a role.
- `pricing:*` is unmapped on purpose. It crosses modules — the Billing price book hosts
  both facility tariff rows and pharmacy retail rows — so mapping it would break the
  cross-module screen. It is gated by role and by the host screen's own module.

## ABAC

- Scope covers tenant, facility, department, unit, ward, room, bed, ownership, assignment,
  shift, and status.
- Break-glass must be explicit, time-limited, and audited (`break_glass:*`).
- Every permission decision must be recordable and auditable.

## Accounts (books desk)

- Keys: `accounts:read`, `accounts:write`. Domain `accounts` → module `facility-accounts`
  (same pattern as `billing` → `billing-payments`), BASIC tier.
- Route `/accounts`: (`accounts:read` ∪ `accounts:write`) ∩ `facility-accounts`. Fallback
  tab when other sections are unauthorized: Open work.
- Write (Journal / Post / Reverse / Void / Send / Open period / Close period / chart
  mutate): `accounts:write`.
- Approve / Reject: `accounts:write` ∩ `financial:approve`. Note `financial:approve` maps
  to `billing-payments` and is capped at ADVANCED, so approval needs Advanced even though
  the Accounts desk itself opens at Basic.
- Patient ledgers browse: `accounts:read`. Pay deep-link only: `billing:write` ∩
  `billing-payments` — do not invent an accounts-only pay.
- Do not grant Accounts via `hr:read` / `hr:write` alone. Billing cashier (`billing:*`)
  does not imply Accounts keys.
- Unauthorized Accounts tabs/actions must be absent, not disabled "no access" chrome. See
  `prompts/02-accounts/01-permissions.md`.

## Enforcement

- UI, API, menu, route, component, and workflow access must pass effective-access checks.
- Backend is authoritative; UI hide/disable alone is never enough. Every screen needs a
  matching API check.
- Permission/role/module/subscription changes must be atomic, versioned, and auditable.
- Failed changes must roll back completely.

## Canonical Files

- `backend/src/config/permissions.js`, `backend/src/config/roles.js`
- `backend/src/lib/authorization/effective-access.js`, `permission-module-map.js`,
  `permission-read-dependency.js`
- `backend/src/lib/subscriptions/subscription-permission-caps.js`, `plan-module-matrix.js`
- `frontend/lib/core/permissions/*` (`app_permission.dart`, `access_policy.dart`,
  `permission_module_map.dart`, `plan_permission_caps.dart`, `commercial_module_tiers.dart`,
  `route_access_catalog.dart`)

## Testing note

`frontend/test/flutter_test_config.dart` sets `VersionDisabledPermissions.enforce = false`
for the whole `test/` suite, so deferred-screen feature tests can still exercise their
permission matrices. Deferred-domain stripping is therefore **not** asserted by default —
only `version_disabled_permissions_test.dart` re-enables it. Any new test asserting that a
version-disabled key is denied must set `enforce = true` itself.

